  "interpretations": [
    {
      "id": "I1",
      "interpretation": "No Sleep is foundational: without sleep every developmental structure goes to zero.",
      "verdict": "SURVIVED",
      "post_evidence": "A post-fix: theories=0, questions=0, hypotheses=0, dreams=0",
      "reason": "Sleep bypasses every downstream layer by construction; no change in the frequency estimate can resurrect them."
    },
    {
      "id": "I2",
      "interpretation": "Memory Without Structure is foundational: without a structured substrate nothing develops.",
      "verdict": "SURVIVED",
      "post_evidence": "J post-fix: theories=0, hypotheses=0, dreams=0",
      "reason": "The substrate is removed outright; the scope fix cannot affect a condition that never builds a graph."
    },
    {
      "id": "I3",
      "interpretation": "No Lineage is the control: populations are identical to the reference arm and only the lineage metric moves.",
      "verdict": "SURVIVED",
      "post_evidence": "B post-fix populations equal O_FULL post-fix: beliefs=6 vs 6, subjects>=2 max=1 vs 1",
      "reason": "Lineage removal strips parent_ids and cannot change which beliefs are produced."
    },
    {
      "id": "I4",
      "interpretation": "No Falsification FREEZES the organism rather than bloating it: contradiction duty collapses and it produces almost nothing.",
      "verdict": "RETRACTED",
      "post_evidence": "D post-fix: belief pool 18.0/18, subjects>=2 mean/max 6.0/6, MBSD=1.0, retention pressure=1.2 (pre-fix: all zeros)",
      "reason": "The pre-fix zeros were produced by the scope defect, not by removing falsification. Post-fix, No Falsification is the BEST-SUPPLIED condition in the entire study -- 18 beliefs, every subject competing, MBSD 1.000 -- and it is the only V1 condition that passes the launch gates on the study stream. The interpretation 'falsification prevents freeze' is withdrawn; the pre-fix evidence for it was an instrumentation artifact."
    },
    {
      "id": "I5",
      "interpretation": "Dreams carry the upper ladder: removing them collapses processes and workflows to zero.",
      "verdict": "SURVIVED (direction), RECALIBRATED (magnitude)",
      "post_evidence": "E post-fix: subjects 4.99, subjects>=2 0.81/2, MBSD 0.163 (pre-fix: 0.07/1, MBSD 0.016)",
      "reason": "E still has almost no subject competition post-fix, so the qualitative claim holds. But the pre-fix magnitude (0.07 subjects with >=2 beliefs) was itself inflated by the defect, and the post-fix figure is higher, so the claim is stated with a different number."
    },
    {
      "id": "I6",
      "interpretation": "EIG is the only producer of investigations and experiments, and removing it RAISES theories, hypotheses and questions while the two output layers go to zero -- it passes G4, but in the wrong direction.",
      "verdict": "SURVIVED",
      "post_evidence": "C post-fix: theories=2, questions=2, hypotheses=14, investigations=0, experiments=0",
      "reason": "The intervention removes layers 7 and 8 outright; the direction of the effect is structural."
    },
    {
      "id": "I7",
      "interpretation": "Questions are not the gateway -- dreams are: removing questions leaves investigations and experiments alive.",
      "verdict": "SURVIVED",
      "post_evidence": "G post-fix: questions=0, investigations=5, experiments=5",
      "reason": "The layer ordering is unchanged by the frequency scope."
    },
    {
      "id": "I8",
      "interpretation": "Random curiosity is genuinely different selection (Jaccard 0.111 vs EIG) and still buys no developmental gain -- EIG is a perfect ranker that buys nothing measurable.",
      "verdict": "SURVIVED (as a V1 finding); the question it poses is now OPEN",
      "post_evidence": "The selection-side facts (Jaccard overlap, top-k precision) are properties of the ranking code, not of the frequency estimate, so they are unaffected. Whether the *developmental* outcome is still flat is exactly what the V2 campaign measures, on a substrate where the belief cap binds.",
      "reason": "A perfect selector over a starved candidate pool cannot matter. Post-fix the pool is no longer starved on the branch stimulus, so the V1 conclusion is not evidence against EIG; it is evidence that the pool was empty."
    },
    {
      "id": "I9",
      "interpretation": "The organism is SUPPLY-limited, not selection-limited: the scarce resource is competing expectations about the same subject, not vocabulary.",
      "verdict": "RETRACTED AS A GENERAL STATEMENT",
      "post_evidence": "On the branch stimulus the pool is 18 beliefs over 7 competing subjects against a cap of 15, and the retention policy changes the retained competing-subject count (7 pre-retention, 5-6 post-retention). Selection is now measurable and the cap binds.",
      "reason": "The claim was true of the study stream on the pre-fix substrate and is the reason the branch stimulus was built. It is not a property of the architecture, and stating it as one would have been the same mistake as the r=4 boundary: reading a property of the instrument as a property of the system."
    },
    {
      "id": "I10",
      "interpretation": "MAX_HYPOTHESES is INERT: the belief cap never binds, so the retention policy cannot matter.",
      "verdict": "RETRACTED AS A GENERAL STATEMENT (still true of the study stream)",
      "post_evidence": "Study stream post-fix: belief pool max 6 against a cap of 15 -- still under, so still inert THERE. Branch stimulus: 18 beliefs against a cap of 15 -- the cap binds and the policy changes the retained population.",
      "reason": "An instrument property, scoped to a stimulus, reported as an architecture property."
    },
    {
      "id": "I11",
      "interpretation": "More vocabulary makes it worse: 42 world tags gave 1 theory and 97 gave 0.",
      "verdict": "SURVIVED",
      "post_evidence": "The stimulus sweep is a comparison between two stimuli on one substrate, so its differential is unaffected by a change to the frequency estimate; the absolute theory counts move, the ordering does not.",
      "reason": "A within-substrate comparison, which is the kind that survives a substrate change."
    }
  ],
